coder › Implemented `RateLimiter` token bucket on branch `work/rate-limiter` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/limiter.ts` (`a3e882a Implement RateLimiter token bucket`): bucket starts full (`tokens = capacity`, `last = now()`); private `refill()` adds `(elapsedMs / 1000) * refillPerSecond` capped at `capacity`; `tryTake(n = 1)` returns `false` without taking when `n > capacity` or fewer than `n` tokens are available, else subtracts and returns `true`; `available` getter refills up to current time and returns the (possibly fractional) balance.
- `src/limiter.test.ts` (`2180eb9 Add RateLimiter token bucket tests`): kept existing `starts full` test, added 5 tests covering burst drain + refuse-without-taking, multi-token take with no partial take, continuous/fractional refill, cap at capacity, and `n > capacity` always refused even after long idle.

Checks:
- Project has only `bun test` (no typecheck/lint scripts in `package.json`).
